WEBVTT

NOTE
Guide narration timing (local Kokoro voice). Regenerate after the ElevenLabs take.

1
00:00:02.935 --> 00:00:06.095
Every industrial site changes by the hour.

2
00:00:06.196 --> 00:00:08.036
Contractors arrive.

3
00:00:08.086 --> 00:00:10.176
Equipment is isolated.

4
00:00:10.226 --> 00:00:11.696
Work moves.

5
00:00:12.065 --> 00:00:15.855
Insurance sets conditions under which risk is accepted.

6
00:00:15.978 --> 00:00:19.888
Good teams translate them into permits, briefings and checklists.

7
00:00:20.543 --> 00:00:23.503
But no one can hold a moving site in mind.

8
00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:28.290
On Roof 03, hot work begins, every safeguard in place.

9
00:00:29.022 --> 00:00:31.662
Then a sprinkler zone goes offline.

10
00:00:33.587 --> 00:00:35.407
Nothing looks different.

11
00:00:35.517 --> 00:00:38.827
The conditions have changed, and nobody sees it.

12
00:00:40.435 --> 00:00:43.646
If something goes wrong, questions begin afterwards:

13
00:00:43.696 --> 00:00:45.336
What was happening?

14
00:00:45.536 --> 00:00:47.576
Which condition applied?

15
00:00:47.676 --> 00:00:49.636
Can you prove what was true?

16
00:00:50.217 --> 00:00:53.357
Today, the gap is often discovered too late.

17
00:00:59.022 --> 00:01:02.352
What if the decision existed when the risk changed?

18
00:01:03.261 --> 00:01:06.251
<v Worker>I'm welding on Roof 03 until six.

19
00:01:06.848 --> 00:01:10.328
Priora connects the work to the conditions that matter.

20
00:01:11.739 --> 00:01:15.629
It checks the certificate and safeguards, and keeps the record.

21
00:01:15.978 --> 00:01:18.078
Prevention before the work.

22
00:01:18.128 --> 00:01:20.028
Proof as it happens.

23
00:01:21.196 --> 00:01:23.616
The sprinkler goes offline again.

24
00:01:23.666 --> 00:01:26.336
This time, Priora sees it at once.

25
00:01:28.696 --> 00:01:30.606
The risk owner decides:

26
00:01:30.656 --> 00:01:32.306
change the work,

27
00:01:33.261 --> 00:01:35.341
knowingly retain the risk,

28
00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:40.366
or, in time, ask selected carriers whether they will cover it.

29
00:01:41.739 --> 00:01:44.839
Every kind of work carries its own conditions.

30
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.720
A crane lift, as the wind picks up.

31
00:01:48.261 --> 00:01:51.361
A gas detector, bypassed for maintenance.

32
00:01:51.848 --> 00:01:55.758
A confined space entry, while the ventilation is down.

33
00:01:56.413 --> 00:01:58.523
Most work stays ordinary.

34
00:01:58.573 --> 00:02:02.533
The few changes that matter become decisions, made in time.

35
00:02:03.271 --> 00:02:06.631
For everyone who carries the risk, the gap closes.

36
00:02:08.152 --> 00:02:09.392
Priora.

37
00:02:09.822 --> 00:02:12.782
Know the risk you carry, while the work happens.
